Homepage: https://github.com/roemer2201/product-rating
Description: self-hostable product ratings by EAN barcode
 product-rating records products by their EAN barcode, together with a photo
 and a rating from zero to five stars. It is built for a household: a handful
 of accounts share one product catalogue, while ratings and photos belong to
 the account that created them. Registration is by invitation code only, and
 the application makes no outgoing network requests of its own.
 .
 The package installs the API server and the built web client, which one
 process serves together, plus a systemd unit, a logrotate rule and the
 product-rating command line tool. Products live in an SQLite database below
 /var/lib/product-rating, photos in the file system next to it, and the
 configuration in /etc/product-rating/config.toml.
 .
 The service listens on the loopback interface by default and expects a
 reverse proxy in front of it that terminates TLS - the camera of the barcode
 scanner needs a secure context in the browser.
